# T009 pre-execution review package — 2026-11-05

D2 contract and D4 parameters are adopted; D3 comparison and D4-deps review are
conditionally authorized by the maintainer. See
[authority](../../decisions/local-persistence-experiment-20261105.md).
D1 stays post-F0/pre-F3/MVP. Network acquisition was separately authorized.
This package contains no candidate encoders and no executed storage trials.
T009 stays open for pre-execution review; product AC-01..07 remain UNVERIFIED.

## Concrete review inputs

- M0.json, M1.json, M32.json, ML.json: full neutral entity/check/operation/payload/
  relationship tables and historical/current states. fixture-hashes.json binds
  materialized raw bytes under `.local/build/persistence-experiment-preflight-20261105/raw/`.
  ML has exactly 125829120 raw input bytes; oracle captures add logical bytes.
- revalidation.json: every affected check/mutation plus full unchanged negative-control
  result set. expected-cases.json: 54 case variants across E01..E08, allowed outcomes,
  paired ordering and external effect/ack counter contract. admission.json: exact
  boundary/+1 arithmetic separately from 1 GiB/4 GiB/512 MiB experiment limits.
- migration-v0/v1/v2.json and migration-expected.json: complete logical version
  fixtures, version guard and target equivalence. These are disposable fixture
  versions, not a claimed historical Ox storage format.
- Cargo.toml/Cargo.lock: exact isolated resolution (272 registry packages plus local
  resolution-only target). native-source.json binds libsqlite3-sys/SQLite/source ID,
  amalgamation hashes, flags from source and technical findings. resolved-dependencies.json
  lists exact versions/source/license declarations and local license-file identities.
- configuration.md: snapshot v1 wire/layout/publication/recovery design, SQLite
  mode/readbacks, explicit transaction/backup/lease rules and unverified mechanics.
- observed-inputs.json/source-observation/: current Engine/controller/UI and product
  lock identities, including existing uncommitted changes. before/ and preconditions.json
  preserve affected documentary preimages; initial-status.txt records existing work.
- environment.json: actual Linux x86_64/Rust 1.99.1/XFS preparation observation.
  Mount options and free bytes must be observed again before trials.

Neutral fixtures encode historical data, including deliberate rejected/timeout states;
they do not assert new execution of the copied /usr/bin/true binary. `/fixture` paths
are logical labels with a recorded future absolute path binding. NOT APPLICABLE is
an explicit disposition: M32 has 26 executed-observation records and six dispositions,
not 32 actual Engine executions. Current Engine admission includes executable bytes
and reserves the whole maximum post-capture. Full-32 product observations remain
covered only by their own existing T903 evidence, not this corpus.

## Primary documentation review

Local downloaded versioned crate sources are primary, content-bound in native-source.json:
rusqlite 0.41.1 backup.rs/transaction.rs/busy.rs and libsqlite3-sys 0.39.1 build.rs,
SQLite 3.54.1 amalgamation. [SQLite 3.54.1 release](https://www.sqlite.org/releaselog/3_54_1.html)
was consulted and matches the source version; [PRAGMA](https://www.sqlite.org/pragma.html),
[rollback atomic commit](https://www.sqlite.org/atomiccommit.html) and
[backup](https://www.sqlite.org/backup.html) are unversioned design references.
They do not establish this host's durability. Versioned docs.rs pages and Rust
1.99.1 File page returned tool access errors; local crate sources are retained.
Rust safe file-lock/sync APIs and effective runtime values require build/runtime
review before trials. Crate MIT texts and SQLite public-domain header are preserved;
transitive license declarations are an inventory, not distribution approval.

Source review found native extension-loading capability enabled by bundled flags;
the Rust load_extension feature is absent. Runtime loading must stay disabled.
Explicitly reset busy timeout to zero; convenience backup retry must not defeat
fail-fast/watchdog. Fresh Iced transitives may differ from application/Cargo.lock:
both candidates share this one isolated lock, and no F0 result transfers to it.
No native build or PRAGMA query was run in this preparation.

## Existing commands for review

From repository root (all commands/tools inspected or executed here):

```bash
python3 docs/validation/persistence-preflight-20261105/verify.py
cargo +1.99.1 metadata --locked --offline --format-version 1 --manifest-path .local/build/persistence-experiment-preflight-20261105/dependencies/Cargo.toml
PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 python3 sdd/tools/validate.py --root . --structure-only
PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 python3 tools/governance/scripts/check-ox.py
git diff --check
```

The offline generate-lockfile attempt failed because rusqlite was absent. After
explicit network permission, isolated cargo fetch resolved/downloaded successfully;
metadata --locked --offline succeeded. Application manifests/lock remain byte-identical
to observed inputs. No nonexistent candidate-run commands are advertised.

## Required pre-run dispositions and limitations

Review the corpus clarification (dispositions vs executions), exact dependency lock,
source/licenses/build-flag design, snapshot publication protocol and expected outcomes.
Freeze this review by package hash before any encoder work. Changing expected values
later requires preserved predecessors and affected-case comparability review.

After review, candidate implementation must expose frozen logical/physical barriers,
external effect/ack logs and the same Iced shell. Build identities/compiler flags,
effective SQLite settings/source ID/compile options, actual snapshot flush/lock calls,
real denied-permission process identity, supervisor implementation and actual-effect
harness binary identities must then be observed before measured trials. Those cannot
be claimed from this non-execution package. No permission for encoders/trials is
inferred from preparing this review. No test result or winner exists.

Real ENOSPC remains UNVERIFIED pending separate authorization of a bounded disposable
filesystem; simulated ENOSPC must be identified separately. No host disk filling or
mount is authorized. Missing critical evidence prevents D5. D6 remains a separate
product integration decision. No commit/publication, automatic cleanup or product
persistence occurred. Raw inputs are local, not self-contained in a Git-only copy;
reviewers must retain the bound owned build directory. No further network permission
is currently missing for the acquisition already performed.

## Observed preparation checks and governance impact

Neutral manifest/reference/raw-byte/source/lock checks passed, including four
negative controls. Structure-only SDD passed. The global check-ox check failed:
its existing evidence bindings still identify predecessor document bytes changed
by this authorization (project/architecture/open-questions/proposal/protocol and
feature artifacts). Initial archive-relative-link failures were corrected by
retaining preimages as .bin files; raw bytes remain unchanged. Logs retain both
attempts. No old observation hash was renewed to claim fresh acceptance.

Global documentary freshness reconciliation is an explicit outstanding item; it
does not establish a product regression or erase T903 operational measurements.
This step does not claim the global governance gate passed on changed documents.
Reviewers must reconcile affected documentary bindings with successor evidence
before relying on a new global freshness verdict. Operational inputs observed in
this step remain byte-identical. No broad Rust/GUI reruns were performed because
this work changed only preparation/documents and isolated dependency scaffolding.

Shared-oracle review correction: changing the common /fixture/oracle bytes
invalidates every dependent check in that corpus, including the applicability
context. Input/arguments/criterion changes remain per-check. The first table and
its hash ledger are preserved in before/*-first.json.bin; corrected table was
rechecked. This correction precedes any encoder or run; it is not a changed result
after benchmarking. Current before/after negative controls use the explicit
affected_checks set rather than assuming every mutation affects only one record.
